\section*{Arithmetic Stein-degree bounds for log Calabi–Yau boundaries}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
For a projective log Calabi--Yau pair over a characteristic-zero field, the algebraic constants of a boundary component of coefficient at least $t$ are claimed to have degree bounded solely by dimension and $t$. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 034, 2026-09-25): A bounded polarization power descends across a controlled field extension, and strata with integral weights bound Galois orbits of divisorial valuations. If the distinguished divisor becomes vertical in a Mori fibration, a horizontal coefficient-one component and adjunction reduce the dimension.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
